_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 16
---
order: 16
---
short_label: XIII.16
---
red_highlight: yes
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To construct an icosahedron and comprehend it in a sphere, like the aforesaid figures; and to prove that the square on the side of the icosahedron is the irrational straight line called minor.
----
proof:

Set out the diameter {AB} of the given sphere, and cut it at {C} so that {AC} is quadruple {CB}, describe the semicircle {ADB|semiT} on {AB}, draw the straight line {CD} from {C} at right angles to {AB}, and join {DB}. [!just VI.9; I.11]

Set out the circle {EFGHK|Vcirc}, and let its radius be equal to {DB}.  Inscribe the equilateral and equiangular pentagon {EFGHK|EFpent} in the circle {EFGHK|Vcirc}, bisect the circumferences *EF, FG, GH, HK,* and *KE* at the points {L}, {M}, {N}, {O}, and {P}, and join {LM}, {MN}, {NO}, {OP}, {PL}, and  {EP}. [!just IV.11; I.9]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="600" height="400" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XIII.16 diagram" src="propXIII16.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // The diameter AB is cut at C with AC quadruple CB (VI.9) and DB, from
    // the semicircle and the perpendicular CD (I.11), is the radius of the
    // circle EFGHK. The pentagon EFGHK (IV.11) and the arcs bisected at
    // L..P (I.9) give the pentagon LMNOP and the decagon side EP; EQ..KU,
    // set up equal to the radius (XI.12, I.3), give the pentagon QRSTU, and
    // XIII.10 makes the ten band triangles equilateral. VZ through the
    // centre V (III.1, XI.12), cut at W and X, gives the vertices Z and X
    // and the ten cap triangles (XI.6, I.33, IV.15.Cor, XIII.10). XIII.9,
    // VI.8 and III.31 put the icosahedron in a sphere on XZ; XIII.3 and
    // VI.8 make XZ the given diameter; XIII.11 makes the side minor.
    //
    // Joyce's figure is kept and held back until the proof reaches each
    // piece: the circle, the pentagons and decagon, EQ..KU, the ten band
    // triangles (revealed at the joins), XZ and the joins QZ, QW, UZ, EV,
    // LV, LX, XM. VZ and VX are drawn from V as solid slide twins (dVZ,
    // dVX), hidden at rest (initiallyHidden), and give way to Joyce's XZ;
    // A', which only the closing argument names, is hidden at rest too.
    //
    // Everything else added is transparent: sphT, the given sphere's
    // outline as a screen circle (a sphere takes no highlight), and semiT,
    // a faceless twin of the semicircle; the segments the text names that
    // the figure draws only as triangle or polygon sides (QR.., QL.., EK,
    // EP, LM.., VW, WZ, ...); the joins VK, WU, MV, EZ, QX, which the text
    // makes and the figure does not draw; the ten band triangles as
    // faceless twins under Joyce's spellings (QPU, QLR, ... — his have
    // fills, raised over the figure when lit, #140); the ten cap triangles;
    // the pentagon QRSTU; the triangles XEZ, VEZ; and semXZ, the circle on
    // XZ through Q, standing for the semicircle carried round. The arcs
    // EF.. bisected at L..P are left untokenized (an arc on a tilted plane
    // is not in the vocabulary). Right angles (red squares): DCB, QEP, QWZ,
    // UWZ, LVX, ZVE, EVX, XEZ, XQZ, as the text calls them right.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B lineSliders and a free,
    // the given sphere's diameter and centre; A0, A3 off-canvas; E
    // (circleSlider) and X (sphereSlider), deferred until the proof reaches
    // them. Every other point is derived and listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["sphere","sphT","a","A","B","AB"];
    var CUT   = GIVEN.concat(["C","AC","CB"]);
    var SEMI  = CUT.concat(["semi","semiT"]);
    var PERP  = SEMI.concat(["D","CD","BD","angC"]);
    var CIRC  = PERP.concat(["Vcirc"]);
    var PENT  = CIRC.concat(["E","F","G","H","K","EFpent","EK"]);
    var BIS   = PENT.concat(["L","M","N","O","P"]);
    var JLM   = BIS.concat(["LMpent","EP","LM","MN","NO","OP","PL"]);
    var DEC   = JLM.concat(["dec"]);
    var UPL   = DEC.concat(["EQ","FR","GS","HT","KU"]);
    var UPP   = UPL.concat(["Q","R","S","T","U"]);
    var BAND  = ["LQR","MRS","NST","OUT","QUP","LMR","MNS","NOT","POU","LPQ"];
    var BANDT = ["QPU","QLR","RMS","SNT","TOU","QLP","LRM","MSN","NTO","OUP"];
    var JOIN  = UPP.concat(BAND).concat(BANDT).concat(["QR","RS","ST","TU",
                 "QU","QL","LR","RM","MS","SN","NT","TO","OU","PU","QP"]);
    var PQR   = JOIN.concat(["QRSTU"]);
    var RQE   = PQR.concat(["angQEP"]);
    var CEN   = RQE.concat(["V"]);
    var VZX   = CEN.concat(["dVZ","dVX","VZ","VX"]);
    var CUTW  = CEN.concat(["XZ","VZ","VX","W","X","Z","VW","WZ"]);
    var J2    = CUTW.concat(["QZ","QW","UZ","EV","LV","LX","XM"]);
    var RQW   = J2.concat(["angQWZ"]);
    var JVK   = RQW.concat(["VK","WU"]);
    var RUW   = JVK.concat(["angUWZ"]);
    var CAPZ  = RUW.concat(["QUZ","QRZ","RSZ","STZ","TUZ"]);
    var RLV   = CAPZ.concat(["angLVX"]);
    var JMV   = RLV.concat(["MV"]);
    var CAPX  = JMV.concat(["LMX","MNX","NOX","OPX","PLX"]);
    var ICO   = BANDT.concat(["QUZ","QRZ","RSZ","STZ","TUZ",
                 "LMX","MNX","NOX","OPX","PLX"]);
    var RV2   = CAPX.concat(["angZVE","angEVX"]);
    var JEZ   = RV2.concat(["EZ","XEZ","VEZ","angXEZ","XW"]);
    var JQX   = JEZ.concat(["QX","angXQZ"]);
    var SEMX  = JQX.concat(["semXZ"]);
    var BISW  = SEMX.concat(["A'","ZA'","A'W"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
